    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
      {
        "@value": "DICT is required in all AGS4 files where user defined groups and/or headings are specified (Rule 18).\nDICT_STAT defines the status of the heading. This shall contain the data 'KEY', 'REQUIRED', 'KEY+REQUIRED' or 'OTHER', where OTHER denotes the data field is neither key nor required (Rule 10).\nDICT_PGRP allows for inclusion of the parent group name when the DICT_TYPE is \"GROUP\". This permits data integrity checking where data files include user defined groups.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      {
        "@value": "Group rules: If the DICT_TYPE is HEADING, there shall be data variables present for DICT_GRP, DICT_HDNG, DICT_STAT, DICT_UNIT, DICT_DTYP and DICT_DESC.\nIf the DICT_TYPE is GROUP, there shall be data variables present for DICT_GRP and DICT_DESC and the DICT_HDNG, DICT_STAT, DICT_DTYP and DICT_UNIT headings shall contain NULL values.\nData type for data field heading DICT_UNIT shall not be changed from PU.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
